{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of DX-A2 at head 06bb88c83418b9d51c61b95119862310c41faaf2, tree adcc2fe3, for request 1c124ebf and review request 4435eb5b. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nUnder ruling d2bbd4c1, this review covers the merge of main c8c7b631, the two regenerated bundles, the repinned seals, the `docs/scopes.md` sentence and gate 7. Approval d45fb4c5 covers the reviewed DX-A2 source, and this review doesn't read that source again. The named departure stands under ruling f71e8a29: below the floor, the `archived` answer precedes a minimum's kind or incarnation mismatch.\n\nI read the note first, then the merge.\n\n## The merge\n\n- `git show --remerge-diff` on merge aaf902f2 shows hand changes in three paths only: `apps/room/page/assets.ts`, `packages/mcp/src/views/generated.ts` and `scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs`. Every other path is the automatic merge.\n- The head changes the same 55 paths from main that e38f9cc4 changed from its old base, so the merge adds no path and loses none.\n- The resolved seals are the parser's values for the merged source. `security-entry-points.test.mjs` compares them with the source, and it passes 10 of 10 at this head.\n- Both bundles match their source. In a scratch clone of the worktree, I ran `node packages/mcp/scripts/views.mjs` and `npm run build --workspace @generalbusiness/dap-page`. The SHA-256 of each file stayed the same: `generated.ts` 8d20d3a8 and `assets.ts` a281b761.\n\n## The sentence\n\n`docs/scopes.md` now says: \"For an entry below the archive floor, the existing `archived` answer takes precedence over a minimum's kind or incarnation mismatch.\" This is the ruling's sentence, in the place that it asked for. The note says what doesn't change: route-scope validation and authentication still come first.\n\n## The gate\n\n- Gate 7 at aaf902f2, tree d44e7fd3, passes all five stages. Receipt cb1890e4 exits 0 with complete capture, and the same head, tree and tracked source before and after. Node passes 84 cases, Counting 56, Plain 3,192 with one skip and Native 879 with two skips.\n- Ruling d2bbd4c1 put J4 V12 before this gate. Survey 823821be released it after V12's policy step closed.\n- From aaf902f2 to the head, only the note and the manifest change, which the documents-only rule in `docs/testing.md` covers.\n- Gates 1 to 6 stay as the note records them. The note also keeps its earlier failed commands and the failed first preparation of this integration.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The worktree is clean. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main c8c7b631 gives the head tree adcc2fe3.\n- The 55 artifacts name exactly the 55 changed paths, all at this head.\n- I ran these once each, and the worktree stayed clean:\n  - client `read-minimum` and `commons`: 11 of 11;\n  - MCP `commons`: 4 of 4.\n- `check-kernel-boundary`: 127 production sources, 0 refusals.\n- The evidence verifies. The manifest has SHA-256 d861d003. Its 129 cited files match by size and SHA-256. The directory has 2,389 files and 478,818,524 bytes, its `SHA256SUMS` has digest 7052b194 and reruns clean, and no file is writable.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 774 links, 0 broken.\n- check-notes from main: 0 warnings. check-commit-messages: 15 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check`: clean.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. The documentation rewrite at dfe69293 also changes `docs/scopes.md`, `docs/kernel.md` and `docs/mcp.md`. Whichever lands second reconciles by hand. Ruling f71e8a29 gives that work to the rewrite's owner.\n2. The deferred waiter cap stays with the planner, as the note says.\n3. The note still uses \"Root\" for the builder and runs some terms together.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe merge changes no design, and the kernel additions stay as approved. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\nThe seals now describe the merged source, so the tripwires work again for both slices. The merge adds no authority and changes no refusal, and the below-floor departure stays within the ruling. Approved.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe merge adds no code beyond generated output and seal values. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: the merged bundles and seals, the `archived` precedence sentence, full gate 7 and the documents-only tail all hold.\n- No Worker deployment follows from this approval. Ruling f71e8a29 holds deployment until the J4 live witness closes.\n- The landing needs a fresh merge-tree check, as the same ruling says, and a subject of at most 100 code points.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:12d63655e5a702507984c484536b58ad57566796","binding":"assigned","head":"06bb88c83418b9d51c61b95119862310c41faaf2","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4cccfc4aa3869cd051bf2d2bc8807d2195438eb7\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:28df5171acd1320942be751570e7a2b044a541e1\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f8a6e28ee8081a9cdbcbbfd79cfa62dafc02862b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}